<%# locals: (path:, title:, description:, value:, state: nil, state_title: nil, bar_percent: nil, locked: false) %>
<%# One row of the hub's list (doc/ki_uebersicht_zeilenliste_plan.md, Nachtrag 2).

    A way to a sub-page, not a display board: name and one line of description on the
    left, the value on the right, a chevron at the end. Five values end on one right
    edge, so the eye runs down instead of across.

    The value column has a MINIMUM width, not a fixed one (min-w-[148px], nowrap): a
    figure is never cut, because half a number is wrong, while a cut name is still
    recognisable. So the name and the description are the parts that give way, each
    kept to one line — two lines of description turn a directory into a reading
    distance that competes with the value. Whoever needs the full description gets it
    on hover (title). The list itself is capped by show.html.erb.

    A dot appears only on a row where something needs doing (:attention, amber) or is
    broken (:alert, red). A running indexing or switch is the normal case and gets no
    colour. The dot's data-row-state is what the request spec reads. No icons: all
    five rows are the same kind of thing, an icon would distinguish nothing.

    The chevron is muted, not faint: it is the only sign that marks the row as a way,
    and it has to read without hover.

    locked: renders the row visible but not as a link — the second face of §3.2 of the
    navigation plan, where AI is off and a prospect must still see what the area holds.
    A locked row keeps a blank of the chevron's width so its value ends on the same
    right edge as the others. %>
<% row_classes = 'flex items-center gap-4 py-[13px] -mx-2 px-2 rounded-sm' %>
<% body = capture do %>
  <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
    <p class="flex items-center text-sm font-medium <%= locked ? 'text-muted' : 'text-heading' %>">
      <span class="truncate"><%= title %></span>
      <% if state %>
        <span class="ml-2 inline-block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full <%= state == :alert ? 'bg-red-600' : 'bg-amber-600' %>"
              role="img" aria-label="<%= state_title %>" title="<%= state_title %>"
              data-row-state="<%= state %>"></span>
      <% end %>
    </p>
    <p class="mt-0.5 truncate text-xs leading-[1.45] <%= locked ? 'text-faint' : 'text-muted' %>"
       title="<%= description %>"><%= description %></p>
  </div>
  <div class="min-w-[148px] shrink-0 text-right">
    <p class="whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] text-body"><%= value %></p>
    <% if bar_percent %>
      <%# 4 px, the same form as the subtask progress: a groove in the selected tone,
          a fill in heading colour, no green, no red. At 0 % the groove stays empty —
          that is a statement too. %>
      <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1 overflow-hidden rounded-sm bg-selected" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="block h-full rounded-sm bg-heading" style="width: <%= bar_percent.clamp(0, 100) %>%"></span>
      </span>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <% if locked %>
    <span class="h-[11px] w-[11px] shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <% else %>
    <svg class="h-[11px] w-[11px] shrink-0 text-muted" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
         stroke-width="2.1" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6" /></svg>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
<li class="border-b border-cream-200">
  <% if locked %>
    <div class="<%= row_classes %>" aria-disabled="true"><%= body %></div>
  <% else %>
    <%# Hover lifts the row to the content surface (white in the default theme), because
        the list lies directly on the shell ground (surface-shell, cream-100): the brief's
        "Hover cream-100" IS that ground here, measured, and painted nothing. %>
    <%= link_to path, class: "#{row_classes} hover:bg-surface focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-black focus-visible:ring-offset-2" do %>
      <%= body %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</li>
